\draw (-2,0) -- (2,0);
\draw (0,-2) -- (0,2);
\node at (1,1.25) {$A$};
\node[font=\small] at (1,0.75) {all $+$};
\node at (-1,1.25) {$S$};
\node[font=\small] at (-1,0.75) {$\sin +$};
\node at (-1,-0.75) {$T$};
\node[font=\small] at (-1,-1.25) {$\tan +$};
\node at (1,-0.75) {$C$};
\node[font=\small] at (1,-1.25) {$\cos +$};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,1.8) {$1$};
\node[font=\small] at (-1.8,1.8) {$2$};
\node[font=\small] at (-1.8,-1.8) {$3$};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,-1.8) {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The acute reference angle is $\alpha=\sin^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)=\frac{\pi}{4}$.

Sine is negative in quadrants 3 and 4.

$\begin{align*}x&=\pi+\frac{\pi}{4}=\frac{5\pi}{4}\\x&=2\pi-\frac{\pi}{4}=\frac{7\pi}{4}\end{align*}$

